---
// 1873 — The Unification section
// Historical moment: Buda, Obuda, and Pest merged into Budapest on November 17, 1873
---

<section
  id="unification"
  class="relative min-h-dvh overflow-hidden bg-inverted py-section palette-surface-primary"
  aria-labelledby="unification-heading"
  data-unification
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center">
      <!-- Giant year -->
      <span
        class="font-display text-figure font-black leading-none tracking-tight text-inverted-foreground/[0.06] sm:text-[clamp(5rem,4rem+6vw,12rem)]"
        aria-hidden="true"
        data-unification-year
      >
        1873
      </span>

      <h2
        id="unification-heading"
        class="mt-6 max-w-heading font-display text-headline-1 font-bold leading-[1.05] text-inverted-foreground sm:mt-8"
      >
        Three Became One
      </h2>

      <p
        class="mt-6 max-w-lg text-base leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/60 sm:text-lg"
      >
        On November 17, 1873, three separate cities — Buda, Obuda, and Pest —
        merged to form a single capital. The unification transformed a
        fragmented landscape into one of Europe's great metropolises.
      </p>

      <!-- Three city names -->
      <div
        class="mt-16 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-8 sm:mt-24 sm:gap-12"
        data-unification-cities
      >
        <div class="reveal text-center" data-city-word="buda">
          <span
            class="block font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground"
          >
            Buda
          </span>
          <span
            class="mt-1 block text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-inverted-foreground/30"
          >
            Western hills
          </span>
        </div>

        <span class="text-2xl text-inverted-foreground/20" aria-hidden="true"
          >+</span
        >

        <div class="reveal text-center" data-city-word="obuda">
          <span
            class="block font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground"
          >
            Obuda
          </span>
          <span
            class="mt-1 block text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-inverted-foreground/30"
          >
            Ancient quarter
          </span>
        </div>

        <span class="text-2xl text-inverted-foreground/20" aria-hidden="true"
          >+</span
        >

        <div class="reveal text-center" data-city-word="pest">
          <span
            class="block font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground"
          >
            Pest
          </span>
          <span
            class="mt-1 block text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-inverted-foreground/30"
          >
            Eastern plains
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Arrow / equals -->
      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col items-center sm:mt-16" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="h-16 w-px bg-inverted-foreground/10 sm:h-24"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- BUDAPEST result -->
      <span
        class="mt-8 block font-display text-headline-1 font-black uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-inverted-foreground sm:mt-12 sm:text-[clamp(2.5rem,2rem+3vw,5rem)]"
        data-unification-result
      >
        Budapest
      </span>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/40">
        November 17, 1873
      </p>

      <!-- Historical context -->
      <div
        class="reveal mt-16 grid max-w-4xl gap-8 text-left sm:mt-24 sm:grid-cols-3"
      >
        <div>
          <span
            class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground/15"
          >
            1873
          </span>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/50">
            Buda, Obuda, and Pest became one capital through a civic merger
            formally completed on November 17, 1873.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span
            class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground/15"
          >
            1896
          </span>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/50">
            Hungary's millennial celebrations reshaped public space around
            Andrassy Avenue and the Millennium Underground Railway, opened in
            1896.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span
            class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-inverted-foreground/15"
          >
            9
          </span>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inverted-foreground/50">
            The Chain Bridge had already opened in 1849, making the idea of one
            city visible across the Danube before the cities legally merged.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
